"lib/runner.kfx: runners, in KFX (PLAN.md section 6.1; after Coopt's
 docs/research/runners.md, and Ahman and Bauer's runners). A program
 performs an operation on the outside world by suspending to its runner's
 prompt with the operation and its rest; the runner answers, and resumes
 it. What answers is the runner's choice:

   sim     a script of input and a clock that moves a tick an operation;
   record  another runner, each operation and its answer kept, in order;
   replay  the answers a record kept, each operation checked against the
           one recorded there: a run that parts from its log fails at the
           first step it parts, saying where.

 A run's only inputs are the answers; its outputs (what it writes) are
 operations, checked on replay, not stored apart. The live runner, the
 world's own answers, needs I/O FX-26 has not: raised with the user
 (PLAN.md section 8).

 Generic in what the program may do besides, `u`; `w` is the runner's
 region, where its tag and its state are."

"An operation, and its answer. A failure's answer is the system's words
 (an `io-error`'s detail, for a live runner)."
(define-type op (sumof (read-line unit) (write string) (clock unit) (read-file string)
                       (write-file (productof (path string) (text string)))))
(define-type answer (sumof (line string) (eof unit) (done unit) (time i64) (text string) (failed string)))

"A program's rest, given the answer, resumable once."
(define-type (rest (a type) (u effect) (w region))
  (subr (maxeff u (read @globals) spin (read w) (write w) (alloc w) (goto w) (comefrom w)) (answer) a))

"What a program gives its runner: an operation and its rest."
(define-type (request (a type) (u effect) (w region)) (productof (op op) (k (rest a u w))))

(define-type (runner-tag (a type) (u effect) (w region))
  (prompt-tag a (request a u w) (maxeff u (read @globals) spin (read w) (write w) (alloc w) (goto w) (comefrom w)) w))

"A program: what it does, and its answer."
(define-type (program (a type) (u effect) (w region))
  (subr (maxeff u (read @globals) spin (read w) (write w) (alloc w) (goto w) (comefrom w)) ((runner-tag a u w)) a))

"An operation performed: the program suspended, the runner given it."
(define perform! (poly ((a type) (u effect) (w region))
                   (subr (maxeff u (read @globals) spin (read w) (write w) (alloc w) (goto w) (comefrom w)) ((runner-tag a u w) op) answer))
  (plambda ((a type) (u effect) (w region))
    (lambda (rt o)
      (abort-with-continuation rt (lambda ((k (rest a u w))) (product (op o) (k k)))))))

"The operations, as a program writes them."
(define read-line! (poly ((a type) (u effect) (w region))
                     (subr (maxeff u (read @globals) spin (read w) (write w) (alloc w) (goto w) (comefrom w)) ((runner-tag a u w)) answer))
  (plambda ((a type) (u effect) (w region))
    (lambda (rt) ((proj perform! a u w) rt (sum read-line #u)))))

(define write! (poly ((a type) (u effect) (w region))
                 (subr (maxeff u (read @globals) spin (read w) (write w) (alloc w) (goto w) (comefrom w)) ((runner-tag a u w) string) unit))
  (plambda ((a type) (u effect) (w region))
    (lambda (rt s) (begin ((proj perform! a u w) rt (sum write s)) #u))))

(define clock! (poly ((a type) (u effect) (w region))
                 (subr (maxeff u (read @globals) spin (read w) (write w) (alloc w) (goto w) (comefrom w)) ((runner-tag a u w)) i64))
  (plambda ((a type) (u effect) (w region))
    (lambda (rt)
      (tagcase ((proj perform! a u w) rt (sum clock #u))
        (time t t)
        (else other -1)))))

"An entry of a record: the step, the operation, its answer."
(define-type entry (productof (step i64) (op op) (answer answer)))
(define-type (log (w region)) (listof entry w))

"How a runner answers: given the step and the operation, the answer."
(define-type (answerer (u effect) (w region))
  (subr (maxeff u (read @globals) spin (read w) (write w) (alloc w)) (i64 op) answer))

"A program run under a runner, `answer` answering each operation in turn;
 the step, the operations' count, kept at `steps`. Its prompt does not
 delimit (what it is given names the runner's region), so it has control
 on `w`, as Fixpt's examples' loops have."
(define serve (poly ((a type) (u effect) (w region))
                (subr (maxeff u (read @globals) spin (read w) (write w) (alloc w) (goto w) (comefrom w))
                      ((runner-tag a u w) (answerer u w) (ref i64 w) (request a u w))
                      a))
  (plambda ((a type) (u effect) (w region))
    (lambda (rt answer steps req)
      (let ((n (get steps)))
        (begin
          (set steps (i64+ n 1))
          (prompt rt ((extract req k) (answer n (extract req op)))
                  (lambda ((next (request a u w))) ((proj serve a u w) rt answer steps next))))))))

(define run-under (poly ((a type) (u effect) (w region))
                    (subr (maxeff u (read @globals) spin (read w) (write w) (alloc w) (goto w) (comefrom w))
                          ((answerer u w) (program a u w))
                          a))
  (plambda ((a type) (u effect) (w region))
    (lambda (answer body)
      (let ((rt (the (runner-tag a u w) (make-continuation-prompt-tag)))
            (steps (the (ref i64 w) (new 0))))
        (prompt rt (body rt)
                (lambda ((req (request a u w))) ((proj serve a u w) rt answer steps req)))))))

"The sim: input a script of lines, read in order, then `eof`; writes
 kept at `out`, the latest first; the clock a tick an operation. It has
 no files: a read fails, a write is done and kept nowhere."
(define sim (poly ((u effect) (w region))
              (subr (alloc w) ((ref (listof string w) w) (ref (listof string w) w)) (answerer u w)))
  (plambda ((u effect) (w region))
    (lambda (input out)
      (lambda ((n i64) (o op))
        (tagcase o
          (read-line x
            (let ((lines (get input)))
              (if (null? lines)
                  (sum eof #u)
                  (begin (set input (cdr lines)) (sum line (car lines))))))
          (write s (begin (set out (cons s (get out))) (sum done #u)))
          (clock x (sum time n))
          (read-file p (sum failed "the sim has no files"))
          (write-file f (sum done #u)))))))

"A runner recorded: `inner`'s answers, each kept at `log` with its step
 and operation, the latest first."
(define recording (poly ((u effect) (w region))
                    (subr (alloc w) ((answerer u w) (ref (log w) w)) (answerer u w)))
  (plambda ((u effect) (w region))
    (lambda (inner log)
      (lambda ((n i64) (o op))
        (let ((x (inner n o)))
          (begin (set log (cons (product (step n) (op o) (answer x)) (get log))) x))))))

(define same-op? (subr pure (op op) bool)
  (lambda (x y)
    (tagcase x
      (read-line u (tagcase y (read-line v #t) (else other #f)))
      (write s (tagcase y (write t (string=? s t)) (else other #f)))
      (clock u (tagcase y (clock v #t) (else other #f)))
      (read-file p (tagcase y (read-file q (string=? p q)) (else other #f)))
      (write-file f (tagcase y (write-file g (and (string=? (extract f path) (extract g path))
                                                  (string=? (extract f text) (extract g text))))
                      (else other #f))))))

(define show-op (subr pure (op) string)
  (lambda (o)
    (tagcase o
      (read-line u "read-line")
      (write s (string-append "write " s))
      (clock u "clock")
      (read-file p (string-append "read-file " p))
      (write-file f (string-append "write-file " (extract f path))))))

"A record replayed: its answers, in order, each operation checked against
 the one recorded at its step. Parting from the log is an error that says
 where; so is running past its end."
(define replaying (poly ((u effect) (w region))
                    (subr (alloc w) ((ref (log w) w)) (answerer u w)))
  (plambda ((u effect) (w region))
    (lambda (log)
      (lambda ((n i64) (o op))
        (let ((es (get log)))
          (if (null? es)
              (begin (error (string-append "replay: past the log's end, at step " (i64->string n))) (sum eof #u))
              (let ((e (car es)))
                (if (and (i64= (extract e step) n) (same-op? (extract e op) o))
                    (begin (set log (cdr es)) (extract e answer))
                    (begin (error (string-append "replay: the run parts from its log at step " (string-append (i64->string n)
                                    (string-append ": the log has " (string-append (show-op (extract e op))
                                      (string-append ", the run " (show-op o)))))))
                           (sum eof #u))))))))))

"A log as text, and back: the event stream, a line an entry, its fields
 apart by tabs: the step, the operation's kind and its fields, the
 answer's kind and its fields. In a field, a tab, a newline and a
 backslash are written escaped, a backslash before `t`, `n`, or itself."

(define-rec
  (escaped-onto (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin) ((listof char acyclic) (listof char acyclic)) (listof char acyclic))
    (lambda (cs acc)
      "`cs` escaped, onto `acc`, newest first."
      (cond ((null? cs) acc)
            ((char=? (car cs) #\tab) (escaped-onto (cdr cs) (cons #\t (cons #\\ acc))))
            ((char=? (car cs) #\newline) (escaped-onto (cdr cs) (cons #\n (cons #\\ acc))))
            ((char=? (car cs) #\\) (escaped-onto (cdr cs) (cons #\\ (cons #\\ acc))))
            (else (escaped-onto (cdr cs) (cons (car cs) acc)))))))

(define-rec
  (chars-reversed (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin) ((listof char acyclic) (listof char acyclic)) (listof char acyclic))
    (lambda (xs acc) (if (null? xs) acc (chars-reversed (cdr xs) (cons (car xs) acc))))))

(define escaped (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin) ((listof char acyclic)) string)
  (lambda (cs) (list->string (chars-reversed (escaped-onto cs nil) nil))))

(define field (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin) (string) string)
  (lambda (s) (string-append "\t" (escaped (the (listof char acyclic) (string->list s))))))

(define op-text (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin) (op) string)
  (lambda (o)
    (tagcase o
      (read-line u "read-line")
      (write s (string-append "write" (field s)))
      (clock u "clock")
      (read-file p (string-append "read-file" (field p)))
      (write-file f (string-append "write-file" (string-append (field (extract f path)) (field (extract f text))))))))

(define answer-text (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin) (answer) string)
  (lambda (a)
    (tagcase a
      (line s (string-append "line" (field s)))
      (eof u "eof")
      (done u "done")
      (time t (string-append "time" (field (i64->string t))))
      (text s (string-append "text" (field s)))
      (failed s (string-append "failed" (field s))))))

"A log, its entries in order, as text."
(define log-text (poly ((w region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read w)) ((log w)) string))
  (plambda ((w region))
    (lambda (es)
      (if (null? es)
          ""
          (let ((e (car es)))
            (string-append (i64->string (extract e step))
              (string-append "\t" (string-append (op-text (extract e op))
                (string-append "\t" (string-append (answer-text (extract e answer))
                  (string-append "\n" ((proj log-text w) (cdr es)))))))))))))

"Text's fields, a line's at a time: each line a list of its fields,
 unescaped."
(define-type fields (listof string acyclic))
(define-type lines (listof fields acyclic))

(define-rec
  (fields-of (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin) ((listof char acyclic) (listof char acyclic) fields lines) lines)
    (lambda (cs f fs ls)
      "`f` the field so far, its characters newest first; `fs` the line's
       fields so far, newest first; `ls` the lines so far, newest first."
      (cond ((null? cs) (if (and (null? f) (null? fs)) ls (cons (reverse-fields (cons (list->string (reverse-chars f nil)) fs) nil) ls)))
            ((char=? (car cs) #\newline)
             (fields-of (cdr cs) nil nil (cons (reverse-fields (cons (list->string (reverse-chars f nil)) fs) nil) ls)))
            ((char=? (car cs) #\tab) (fields-of (cdr cs) nil (cons (list->string (reverse-chars f nil)) fs) ls))
            ((and (char=? (car cs) #\\) (not (null? (cdr cs))))
             (fields-of (cdr (cdr cs))
                        (cons (let ((c (car (cdr cs)))) (cond ((char=? c #\t) #\tab) ((char=? c #\n) #\newline) (else c))) f)
                        fs ls))
            (else (fields-of (cdr cs) (cons (car cs) f) fs ls)))))
  (reverse-chars (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin) ((listof char acyclic) (listof char acyclic)) (listof char acyclic))
    (lambda (xs acc) (if (null? xs) acc (reverse-chars (cdr xs) (cons (car xs) acc)))))
  (reverse-fields (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin) (fields fields) fields)
    (lambda (xs acc) (if (null? xs) acc (reverse-fields (cdr xs) (cons (car xs) acc))))))

(define digits (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin) ((listof char acyclic) i64) i64)
  (lambda (cs n)
    (if (null? cs) n (digits (cdr cs) (i64+ (i64* n 10) (i64- (char->i64 (car cs)) 48))))))

(define number-of (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin) (string) i64)
  (lambda (s)
    (let ((cs (the (listof char acyclic) (string->list s))))
      (if (and (not (null? cs)) (char=? (car cs) #\-)) (i64- 0 (digits (cdr cs) 0)) (digits cs 0)))))

"An entry from a line's fields; a line that is none is an error that says so."
(define entry-of (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin) (fields) entry)
  (lambda (fs)
    (let* ((n (number-of (car fs)))
           (k (car (cdr fs)))
           (rest (cdr (cdr fs)))
           (o (the op (cond ((string=? k "read-line") (sum read-line #u))
                            ((string=? k "write") (sum write (car rest)))
                            ((string=? k "clock") (sum clock #u))
                            ((string=? k "read-file") (sum read-file (car rest)))
                            ((string=? k "write-file") (sum write-file (product (path (car rest)) (text (car (cdr rest))))))
                            (else (begin (error (string-append "a log's line names no operation: " k)) (sum clock #u))))))
           (after (if (or (string=? k "read-line") (string=? k "clock")) rest
                      (if (string=? k "write-file") (cdr (cdr rest)) (cdr rest))))
           (j (car after))
           (a (the answer (cond ((string=? j "line") (sum line (car (cdr after))))
                                ((string=? j "eof") (sum eof #u))
                                ((string=? j "done") (sum done #u))
                                ((string=? j "time") (sum time (number-of (car (cdr after)))))
                                ((string=? j "text") (sum text (car (cdr after))))
                                ((string=? j "failed") (sum failed (car (cdr after))))
                                (else (begin (error (string-append "a log's line names no answer: " j)) (sum eof #u)))))))
      (product (step n) (op o) (answer a)))))

"A log from its text: the entries in order."
(define log-of-text (poly ((w region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (alloc w)) (string) (log w)))
  (plambda ((w region))
    (lambda (s)
      (letrec ((go (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (alloc w)) (lines (log w)) (log w))
                 (lambda (ls acc) (if (null? ls) acc (go (cdr ls) (cons (entry-of (car ls)) acc))))))
        (go (fields-of (the (listof char acyclic) (string->list s)) nil nil nil) nil)))))
